.TH DOCKSTAR 1 "July 2026" "Dockstar" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dockstar \- display docking automation for KDE Plasma Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dockstar
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dockstar detects approved external displays, applies an atomic Plasma display layout, and runs configured docking actions. Its daemon exposes a versioned session D-Bus API used by the CLI and settings application.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status, devices, diagnose
Show current state, connected outputs, or diagnostic information as JSON.
.TP
.BI allow " DEVICE_ID"
Approve a display for automatic docking.
.TP
.BI deny " DEVICE_ID"
Deny a display.
.TP
.BI trust " all|allowlist|off"
Set the display trust policy.
.TP
.BI mode " extend|mirror|external-only|internal-only"
Set and immediately apply the display layout.
.TP
.B apply
Apply the current profile.
.TP
.BI wake " status|enable|disable|restore"
Inspect or configure hardware wake sources. Changes require administrator authentication.
.TP
.BI config " show|validate [PATH]"
Print or validate configuration.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dockstar/config.json
.br
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dockstar/state.json
.br
.I /etc/dockstar/wake.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR kscreen-doctor (1)
